{
  "run_id": "PMC12985727__expert_context__papers_n10_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The baseline TiVNbTa is a single-phase BCC dendritic alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has approximately 800 MPa yield strength and 40% strain at room temperature.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, baseline TiVNbTa has approximately 330 MPa yield strength and 423 MPa compressive strength.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 0.1–0.5 at.% carbon to TiVNbTa will promote in-situ TiC precipitation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon addition will produce nanoscale TiC precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The TiC precipitates will be coherent with the TiVNbTa BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The TiC precipitates will be uniformly dispersed within the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiC precipitates will strengthen TiVNbTa by pinning dislocations and impeding their motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7",
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitation strengthening will mitigate the loss of TiVNbTa yield strength at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped TiVNbTa could have roughly 50% higher yield strength at 1273 K than the undoped baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7",
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed carbon addition will preserve adequate room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain sufficient ductility for thermal cycling and mechanical integrity.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon-modified alloy will support efficient heat transfer between W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The strengthening and ductility benefits are expected to remain applicable from room temperature to approximately 1273 K under tensile and compressive loading.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keeping the carbon level low should avoid excessive embrittlement or unwanted secondary-phase formation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal carbon concentration, precipitation kinetics, and TiC coherency in TiVNbTa are uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped and undoped TiVNbTa specimens will be processed identically and tested at room temperature and 1273 K.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is falsified if coherent TiC is absent or if the carbon-doped alloy fails to achieve a statistically significant strength improvement without detrimental ductility loss.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
